insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Getting started', 'How to use this manual', 'This is the Chai Green operations manual. It holds how we open, run and close every store.

Head office keeps it up to date. If something here is wrong or missing, tell your manager.

## Where to find things
- Daily safety checks: Today''s checks
- How to make every dish: Recipes
- Food safety records: Records', 1) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Opening and closing', 'Opening the store', 'Starter text — edit to match Chai Green.

1. Arrive at least 45 minutes before opening.
2. Turn off the alarm and switch on the lights, chillers check, urns and coffee machine.
3. Do the Opening checks in the app, one question at a time. Do each check for real: answers that are too quick are flagged to head office.
4. Set up the counter, cake display and menu boards.
5. Brew the first batch of house chai.
6. Unlock the doors on time.', 2) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Opening and closing', 'Closing the store', 'Starter text — edit to match Chai Green.

1. Stop hot food 30 minutes before closing.
2. Clean down the kitchen, coffee machine and chai urns.
3. Label and store all food.
4. Do the Closing checks in the app.
5. Cash up the till.
6. Lock up and set the alarm.', 3) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Food safety', 'Safe temperatures', '## Keep cold food cold
- Chillers: 5°C or below (legal limit 8°C)
- Freezers: -18°C or below

## Keep hot food hot
- Cook to a core temperature of 75°C or above
- Hot-hold at 63°C or above, for no more than 2 hours
- Reheat once only, to 75°C

## Cooling
- Cool hot food within 90 minutes, then chill it

If a reading is outside these limits, the app tells you what to do and records what you did.', 4) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Food safety', 'Allergens', 'Every dish has its allergens on its recipe card. Never guess.

1. Ask every customer if they have an allergy.
2. Check the recipe card or allergen matrix.
3. If you are unsure, tell the customer you cannot guarantee the dish is safe.
4. Make allergy orders separately, with clean boards, knives and gloves.

The 14 allergens: celery, cereals containing gluten, crustaceans, eggs, fish, lupin, milk, molluscs, mustard, tree nuts, peanuts, sesame, soya, sulphites.', 5) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Food safety', 'Personal hygiene', '- Wash your hands before work, after breaks, after the toilet, after touching raw food and after taking out rubbish.
- Clean uniform every shift, hair tied back, no jewellery except a plain band.
- Tell your manager if you have been sick or had diarrhoea. Do not come to work until 48 hours after it stops.', 6) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Food safety', 'When the Environmental Health Officer visits', '1. Welcome them and tell the manager straight away.
2. Give them access to the Records page in the app: every check, temperature and fix is there, signed by name.
3. Show them the allergen matrix and recipe cards.
4. Write down anything they ask you to improve and tell head office the same day.', 7) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Cleaning', 'Cleaning schedule', 'Starter text — edit to match Chai Green.

## Every day
- Work surfaces, boards and equipment: clean and sanitise after every use
- Floors, toilets, bins: end of day
## Every week
- Chillers and freezers inside, shelves, extraction filters
## Every month
- Deep clean behind and under equipment (checked in the monthly audit)', 8) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Stock and ordering', 'Ordering stock', 'Stock is ordered and sent out through the Chai Green stock app.

- Most products arrive 4 days after ordering; packaging takes up to 3 months, so order early.
- Desserts, milkshake ingredients and most food come from Brakes.
- Rotate stock: first in, first out.
- Write down all waste.', 9) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Brand standards', 'Uniform and presentation', 'Starter text — edit to match Chai Green.

- Full Chai Green uniform, clean every shift
- Name badge worn
- Every dish must match the photo and plating notes on its recipe card', 10) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
insert into public.manual_pages (section, title, body, sort_order) values ('Customer service', 'Our service standards', 'Starter text — edit to match Chai Green.

- Greet every customer within 30 seconds
- Smile, make eye contact and thank them
- Ask about allergies on every food order
- Deal with complaints straight away and tell the manager', 11) on conflict (section, title) do nothing;
